            <ArticleTitle>An unusual presentation of sarcoidosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1936-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 35-year-old woman with arthralgias and skin lesions suggesting sarcoidosis. No pulmonary lesions were present. The diagnosis was established by histological examination of a swollen and discolored scar. We review the literature of &quot;scar sarcoidosis&quot; and discuss the similarities between this entity and silica granuloma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
